+# CATUI shadPS4 Libretro maintenance
+
+This document is the update contract for an agent or developer changing the
+CATUI heavy core. The core is an isolated Libretro boundary around shadPS4;
+the renderer is Vulkan only. Do not add DirectX, OpenGL, software, or fake
+accuracy options to the CATUI profile unless the upstream implementation is
+actually wired through the boundary.
+
+## Updating upstream safely
+
+Keep the CATUI work as a small patch on top of upstream. Before rebasing,
+record the current revision and preserve unrelated worktree changes:
+
+```text
+cd C:\Users\arthi\Projetos\shadPS4
+rtk git status --short
+rtk git fetch origin
+rtk git log -1 --oneline
+```
+
+After updating, inspect conflicts instead of resetting the worktree. The
+CATUI-owned seam is limited to `src/libretro/`, `src/core/catui_runtime.h`,
+and the narrowly required lifecycle/readback changes in the emulator, SDL
+window, signal, and Vulkan presenter paths. Keep the Libretro API free of
+upstream-private types and keep the owner thread responsible for all shadPS4
+window/renderer work.
+
+## Build and validation
+
+Configure or reuse the clang-cl build directory, then build the DLL and both
+smoke/probe targets:
+
+```text
+rtk "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\Common7\IDE\CommonExtensions\Microsoft\CMake\Ninja\ninja.exe" -C build-clang-catui shadps4_libretro catui_shadps4_libretro_smoke catui_shadps4_libretro_real_probe -j 4
+```
+
+Use an extracted title executable, never a PKG as the boot path. PKG/FPKG are
+installation containers: install the base package and every compatible update
+into a title directory, then boot `installed\\<TITLE_ID>-base\\uroot\\eboot.bin`
+with the update overlay `uroot-UPDATE` present. Do not modify or redistribute
+copyrighted package contents.
+
+The mandatory gate is:
+
+1. Vulkan is selected and reported by the environment callback.
+2. The owner thread starts and stops without a hang or callback-after-clear.
+3. At least two decoded PNG frames are visible, non-black, and have different
+   hashes.
+4. Audio callbacks remain active during the run.
+5. `git diff --check` passes in both repositories.
+
+The real probe is a video gate, not a performance result. It validates
+`retro_unload_game` and `retro_deinit` first, then uses an explicit process
+boundary because upstream Vulkan/HLE singletons are process-lifetime objects.
+Do not use that boundary in the Libretro core itself or treat it as a shortcut
+for joining the owner thread.
+
+## CATUI catalog rules
+
+Update `addons/catui-libretros/core_profile_catalog.gd` only with options that
+map to real shadPS4 settings. Current presets vary resolution scale, present
+mode, FSR, and RCAS. Do not reintroduce invented AA, anisotropic filtering,
+CPU/GPU accuracy, multicore, generic scaling, or shader-cache toggles.
+
+Record the upstream commit, compiler, GPU/driver, title ID, app version,
+renderer, frame hashes, and any known title-specific failure in
+`documents/catui-libretro-benchmark.md` and the CATUI `PS4_CORE.md` summary.
