+# CATUI PS4 benchmark protocol
+
+The benchmark is valid only when it records a visible frame. Each run must
+write JSON with the upstream commit, core build ID, renderer, resolution,
+frame count, elapsed milliseconds, average FPS, 1% low FPS, and the SHA-256 of
+the first and last PNG frames.
+
+## Required runs
+
+Run the same title and scene for 30 seconds with:
+
+1. Vulkan / Performance preset;
+2. Vulkan / Balanced preset;
+3. Vulkan / Quality preset;
+4. Software fallback, if the core advertises it.
+
+For every run, assert:
+
+- the core loads and reports a non-zero geometry;
+- at least two non-identical frames arrive;
+- the PNG files decode and are not all black or transparent;
+- audio and video callbacks remain alive until shutdown;
+- shutdown completes without a use-after-free or hanging owner thread.
+
+The Eden standalone executable can be measured with the same wall-clock and
+frame-capture harness for a Switch title, but its numbers must not be merged
+with PS4 results. It cannot boot Gravity Rush 2, which is PS4 content.
+
+## Reproducible command shape
+
+The exact executable names are build-dependent. Record the resolved paths and
+use bounded commands. Never kill an existing user process. A failed launch,
+missing screenshot, or unsupported package is a failed validation, not a zero
+FPS result.
+
+## ABI smoke check
+
+Before a real-title run, build `catui_shadps4_libretro_smoke` with
+`ENABLE_CATUI_LIBRETRO_SMOKE=ON`. It drives the isolated bridge with a
+synthetic backend, requires two non-identical 1280x720 XRGB8888 frames, and
+writes a PPM that can be converted to PNG with FFmpeg. This is a callback and
+lifecycle check only; it must never be reported as a PS4 rendering result.
+
+## Failed Gravity Rush 2 baseline (2026-09-24)
+
+- Source revision: `7910dfe14419f69ff15544dd0129a6de8f6827be` plus the CATUI worktree changes.
+- Compiler: clang-cl 23.1.2, Release x86-64-v3.
+- Renderer: Vulkan 1.3.260, AMD proprietary driver 2.0.279, Radeon RX 580.
+- Content: `CUSA04943`, update 01.11, base `uroot` plus `uroot-UPDATE` overlay.
+- Result: both standalone and the real Libretro probe start Vulkan, audio, game and render threads and compile compute pipelines, then hit exception `0xc0000005` before the first video callback.
+- Image result: the three- and four-second client areas are black; the process has exited by five seconds.
+- Verdict: failed. Do not record zero FPS and do not use the desktop PNG hashes as game-frame evidence.
+
+## Sonic Mania video gate (2026-09-24)
+
+- Content: `CUSA07023`, base 1.01 plus `uroot-UPDATE` app version 1.03.
+- Renderer: Vulkan 1.3.260, AMD proprietary driver 2.0.279, Radeon RX 580.
+- Result: reached the developer/title sequence and produced two distinct,
+  decodable, non-black 1280x720 PNG frames.
+- PNG SHA-256: `F3388AC4B3F6914BC16348AEA748ECC9A1BD1A10C107ADD5BE2F382CDB5C18DF`
+  and `E36AF7C9D06D0AB4CBE7237BF87686DBAD02F1E04E3603B0F9329C21DD18F9B2`.
+- Verdict: video gate passed. The initial probe boundary exposed upstream
