index 00000000..ff05d5e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/documents/catui-libretro.md
@@ -0,0 +1,184 @@
+# CATUI shadPS4 Libretro port
+
+This directory describes the isolated CATUI integration for shadPS4. The
+integration is intentionally kept at the boundary of the emulator: CATUI owns
+the Libretro ABI, controller mapping, frame pacing, and lifecycle, while
+shadPS4 owns PS4 guest execution and Vulkan rendering.
+
+## Current upstream base
+
+The current CATUI work is based on upstream release `v.0.20.0`
+(`529ceb32f5546b820588f194b903cc39d08015fe`, 2026-10-14). Keep the small
+CATUI patch set isolated at the Libretro boundary.
+
+## CATUI Proxy
+
+The Windows isolation system is called **CATUI Proxy**. Its registered DLL
+launches one disposable host process per session and exports
+`retro_get_process_id` for that exact live host. CATUI samples CPU, GPU-engine
+utilization and working-set RAM against this PID, never by window title.
+`retro_get_game_fps` reports the rate of video frames published by the host,
+including publications skipped by frontend polling. This is host video FPS,
+not a guest simulation counter or CATUI presentation FPS. Paused/stopped
+sessions report zero FPS and unavailable host resources. Other cores retain
+the normal in-process metrics path. Keep proxy, host and engine together when
+packaging the store archive.
+
+## Required Libretro contract
+
+The core must export the standard Libretro entry points. The current validation
+implementation retains shadPS4's SDL Vulkan surface because its renderer still
+owns the swapchain; replacing it with the frontend's negotiated Vulkan device
+is required before the hardware fast path is complete. The video callback
+must receive a complete frame before the callback returns. The preferred
+format is `RETRO_PIXEL_FORMAT_XRGB8888`; the fallback is `RGB565`.
+
+## Renderer choice
+
+The CATUI core uses shadPS4's Vulkan renderer. DirectX is not exposed as a
+pretend backend: shadPS4's guest GPU path, shader cache, pipeline cache, and
+image ownership are Vulkan-based upstream. The intended fast path keeps Vulkan
+images on the owner thread and hands them to a compatible CATUI hardware
+session, but it is not implemented yet. The current core copies the composed
+Vulkan image through a staging buffer to XRGB8888 for software-video callbacks
+and mandatory PNG validation. Do not treat readback benchmark numbers as the
+final maximum-performance path.
+
+The frontend supplies:
+
+- Vulkan, OpenGL, or software video through the CATUI session;
+- one DualShock 4 pad per port, including analog sticks, triggers, touchpad
+  click, motion, and rumble;
+- an audio callback with a bounded queue;
+- a content path to an installed `eboot.bin`, `SELF`, `ELF`, or `ZAR`.
+
+`PKG` and `FPKG` are installation containers, not directly bootable content.
+Install the base into `uroot`, install the update into its sibling
+`uroot-UPDATE`, and pass the base `uroot/eboot.bin` to the core. The source
+packages remain unchanged.
+
+The core must report geometry with `retro_get_system_av_info`, keep a stable
+pixel aspect ratio, and return `pitch` in bytes. A frame counter alone is not
+evidence of video: CATUI validation requires a non-null frame, non-zero width
+and height, a changing checksum across two frames, and a saved PNG.
+
+## Performance policy
+
+The CATUI profile defaults to Vulkan, native resolution, persistent pipeline
+caches, FIFO presentation, and Windows static guest-red-zone patching. Only
+settings implemented by the current shadPS4 upstream are advertised: output
+and internal resolution, present mode, VBlank, PS4 Pro mode, FSR/RCAS, HDR,
+GPU selection, pipeline caches, readback/DMA controls, Vulkan diagnostics,
+and motion/touch input. Do not add speculative anti-aliasing, anisotropic,
+CPU/GPU accuracy, async, or latency switches unless upstream gains a real
+setting and the backend applies it.
+
+Do not copy a GPU image to the CPU every frame when a hardware path is active.
+Use a persistent staging/readback resource only for screenshots or when the
+frontend explicitly requests software video. Keep all Vulkan objects on the
+owner thread and defer destruction until the last CATUI frame is released.
+
+## Updating shadPS4 safely
+
+1. Create a fresh worktree at the new upstream commit.
+2. Apply only the CATUI patch series; do not edit generated files or vendored
+   dependencies.
+3. Reconcile changes in emulator startup, renderer ownership, input, and
+   guest memory before compiling the Libretro target.
+4. Build both Debug and Release x86_64 targets.
+5. Run the ABI smoke test, then boot a known-good homebrew ELF or installed
+   title for at least two seconds.
+6. Save the first visible frame and compare its checksum and dimensions with
+   the validation record. A successful process exit without a frame is a
+   failure.
+7. Run the CATUI heavy-core lifecycle test and the benchmark protocol before
+   replacing the installed DLL.
+
+Keep the upstream commit, CATUI patch hash, compiler version, GPU driver,
+game/title ID, and benchmark JSON together. If any check fails, keep the old
+core installed and report the failure instead of silently falling back to an
+unrelated emulator.
+
+## Initial validation record
+
+On 2026-09-23, the supported Windows build path used CMake 4.2.3 and
+clang-cl 23.1.2 with `ENABLE_CATUI_LIBRETRO=ON`. It produced both
+`shadps4.exe` and `shadps4_libretro.dll`. Keep the Clang check before the
+plain `_MSC_VER` check for `PS4_SYSV_ABI`: clang-cl defines `_MSC_VER`, but
+PS4 guest entry points still require `__attribute__((sysv_abi))`. Host
+libraries such as Windows libusb need a narrow host-ABI thunk when they call
+a guest-ABI callback; changing the guest ABI globally causes a crash as soon
+as the first game thread starts.
+
+The isolated `retro_*` ABI was subsequently built and smoke-tested with a
+synthetic backend: two 1280x720 XRGB8888 callbacks arrived through
+`retro_run`, the lifecycle unloaded cleanly, and FFmpeg decoded the captured
+PNG (`SHA-256 7D61B1C37C76E3EA4AAB0DC7D0B1669C6F6C8685C0A4356A987F23E4FC2E443`).
+This proves callback plumbing and image encoding only; it is not evidence that
+shadPS4 booted a PS4 title or that Vulkan guest rendering is connected.
+
+`catui_shadps4_libretro_real_probe` is the real-title gate. It links the actual
+DLL, boots the supplied content path, rejects near-black boot clears, and writes
+the first and last accepted frames as PNG. A missing file, fewer than two
+visible frames, identical hashes, or a non-zero exit is a failed validation.
+
+Gravity Rush 2 (`CUSA04943`) was extracted without modifying the source PKGs.
+The base lives in an `uroot` directory and update 1.11 in the sibling
+`uroot-UPDATE`, matching shadPS4's overlay lookup. The standalone emulator
+recognizes app version 01.11, creates a Vulkan 1.3.260 device on the Radeon RX
+580, initializes video/audio/input, and begins compiling compute pipelines.
+It then raises Windows exception `0xc0000005` after roughly three seconds.
+Desktop captures at three and four seconds show a completely black shadPS4
+client area, and the process is gone by the five-second capture. Therefore no
+real game PNG, FPS result, or benchmark has passed yet. The local firmware
+module directory is also empty and the emulator warns that dumped system
+fonts are missing; retest with legally dumped modules before treating the
+remaining failure as a renderer regression.
+
+At upstream `7910dfe1`, the real Libretro DLL loads the Gravity Rush 2
+`eboot.bin`, selects Vulkan, starts audio/game/render threads, and compiles the
+first compute pipelines. Its real-title probe still terminates with exception
+`0xc0000005` before a video callback arrives; the standalone executable reaches
+the same guest crash. No real non-black PNG or benchmark result is claimed until
+that runtime/title failure is resolved.
+
+The validation machine currently has no legally dumped `sys_modules`, `font`,
+or `font2` data. Before attributing the remaining crash to CATUI, repeat the
+real probe with the upstream-required firmware modules and fonts dumped from
+the user's own PS4. These files must never be downloaded, committed, bundled,
+or copied into a release artifact by the update process.
+
+### Sonic Mania real-title result (2026-09-24)
+
+The user's existing open-source LibOrbisPkg `PkgTool` extracted Sonic Mania
+`CUSA07023` without modifying either source PKG. Base 1.01 is installed at
+`CUSA07023-base/uroot`; update 1.03 is installed at the required sibling
+`CUSA07023-base/uroot-UPDATE`. `param.sfo` and the base icon were extracted
+from their PKG metadata entries because they are outside the inner PFS image.
+
+The real Libretro probe selected Vulkan 1.3.260 on the Radeon RX 580, detected
+app version 01.03, reached the title sequence, and captured two distinct,
+decodable 1280x720 PNGs. Their SHA-256 values are
+`F3388AC4B3F6914BC16348AEA748ECC9A1BD1A10C107ADD5BE2F382CDB5C18DF` and
+`E36AF7C9D06D0AB4CBE7237BF87686DBAD02F1E04E3603B0F9329C21DD18F9B2`.
+This passes the real-video gate. The final probe returns zero after the
+Libretro unload/deinit lifecycle and the 30-second Vulkan benchmarks pass all
+three presets: Performance 39.484 FPS, Balanced 39.144 FPS, and Quality
+39.553 FPS. The harness uses a process boundary only after unload/deinit to
+avoid re-entering upstream process-lifetime singletons during DLL detach.
+
+The final DLL SHA-256 is
+`7b3cb78a85bafe71a6859ba61301bd6a7c2cc9bcd3cd424f34c72e485158a14b`.
+
+Latest retained validation PNGs are `sonic-validation.png` and
+`sonic-validation.last.png`; their SHA-256 values are
+`73cb29e37e79a7a76e39b4ad62588f6e35f2e2b7377f79d22ad1938b00267396` and
+`a5cd31674dc66a8ecba6c3d7a16b22adb7ab3b8d2ec88eb8908475c9d0809c76`.
+
+## Legal and test data
+
+CATUI does not redistribute firmware, keys, PKG/FPKG files, or commercial
+games. A local Gravity Rush 2 package may be used only by the owner of the
+content and only after shadPS4 supports that title. Eden is a Nintendo Switch
+emulator and is not a valid PS4 comparator for Gravity Rush 2; it may be used
+for a separate CATUI heavy-core/frame-pacing smoke benchmark only.
